we've been using and reviewing ipads on  youtube for over four years now  ever since the 2016 9.7 inch ipad pro  back when we were making videos for  apple insider and we've been comparing  samsung galaxy tablets to ipads  ever since we started max tag and  there's one thing  that has never changed apple's ipads  were  always a big step ahead of what samsung  had to offer  but for the last week i've been using  samsung's brand new galaxy tab  s7 and i honestly have to say that i  wasn't expecting it to be  this good so before we dig deep into why  let's talk about how samsung's previous  flagship tab s6  was worse than apple's ipad pro apple  has had 120hz pro motion technology for  the ipad pro  ever since 2017 making it feel so much  more snappy  compared to any samsung tablet then in  2018  apple completely redesigned the ipad pro  with  square edges and a flat back making it  feel  modern and much more premium compared to  samsung's tab s6  apple also added face id to the ipad pro  making it a much better solution  than the under display fingerprint  sensor on the tab s6  which honestly wasn't very convenient  and in terms of performance  the ipad pro was always more powerful  so with that said let's get into the  various ways that i can now confidently  say  that the tab s7 has finally caught up to  the ipad pro  the first major change is that they  completely redesigned the body  with squared off edges instead of  rounded ones  and a completely flat back and even  though samsung  obviously copied the modern design of  the 2018 ipad pro  going as far as to match the same 11  inch display size  i'm glad they did because it honestly  feels so much more premium  and to differentiate it just a bit the  sides now have a brushed metal finish  instead of being matte on the ipad they  also redesigned the s pen wireless  charger on the back  which i think looks really nice one  subtle difference i noticed is that the  speaker grills on the tablet seven  are machined in such a way that it aims  the sound towards the user  which is pretty clever and it seems to  be working because the speakers are  incredible just listen to this  comparison  [Music]  i'm also glad that samsung got rid of  the under display fingerprint sensor  which wasn't very reliable due to having  to get the finger placement  perfect this time samsung instead went  with a simple one built right into the  power button  which is great because you can turn on  the display and authenticate  with a single button press now one thing  i'm very glad samsung upgraded is the  display  it can now refresh at up to 120 hertz  just like the ipad pro this was the  absolute number one feature  that kept the ipad pro ahead for so many  years  and now samsung has finally cut up  apple's version  is still better because the refresh rate  automatically adjusts down to as low as  24 hertz  depending on the content you're viewing  to help save  battery life but now that samsung  finally has 120 hertz  the display feels super smooth and fluid  as you can tell from the slow motion  comparison  filmed at 120 frames per second the  other benefit that surprised me was that  samsung was able to get the latency of  their s pen  down to nine milliseconds matching the  latency of the apple pencil  on the ipad pro that was one of the  things that made the ipad pro  so great and now samsung has finally cut  up on that front as well  now the one issue that i have with  samsung adding this feature is that they  had to sacrifice  their ammo led display technology to add  120 hertz on the 11 inch model  so in terms of the display quality the  ipad pro is now beating out the samsung  in terms of the maximum brightness  the contrast quality and the color  quality as well  as you can see in this comparison now  what's interesting  is that the larger tab s7 plus gets  hertz refresh rate while maintaining the  amoled display  so it's not a hardware limitation they  just chose to leave that feature  to the larger and more expensive model  and that's actually the only difference  between the tab seven and the seven plus  everything else including the chip the  ram and the storage  is identical because of that we didn't  even bother with buying or reviewing  the more expensive tab s7 plus since we  think that most people would rather have  the smaller 11 inch size and to prove  that  we ran a poll asking people which size  they would prefer for  tablets not mentioning any specific  brand name at all  and out of 8 000 people who voted 61  said they would rather buy a smaller  size so it's a bit sad that samsung  didn't include the amoled display on the  11 inch model  but regardless of that it still looks  pretty decent  with high reflectivity being the only  downside that really stands out  now before we get into performance i  want to touch on one final design choice  that samsung actually copied from apple  and i'm so glad that they did samsung  added magnets into the body itself  just like the ipad pro has had since  2018  so now their keyboard cover attaches  magnetically  and it holds on very well just like  apple's magic keyboard case for the ipad  pro  and the ipad air 4. samsung's previous  tab s6  actually had you stick the keyboard case  onto the back of the tablet  which was really annoying and it caused  some issues with  long long-term reliability but now with  those magnets it's completely  fixed and i've got to say that i love  how the keyboard case  completely covers and protects the s-pen  with a flap built into the case  which easily opens up for convenient  access  it also has a flap for angle  adjustability with a really solid metal  hinge  and i really like the material of the  case itself because it seems  so much more resistant to scuffs and  fingerprints than apple's magic keyboard  i also like that you can actually detach  the keyboard while leaving the case on  the back  for drop protection which you can't do  on the magic keyboard  since it's built as one solid piece so  you have to lift the ipad pro  off to more conveniently use it as a  tablet and on the tab s7  you can even fold the keyboard behind  the tablet  if you don't want to completely take it  off so it's super convenient  as far as the keys themselves samsung  upgraded them with a more square shape  and they now honestly feel just a tad  bit better  than the ones on the ipad pro's magic  keyboard case  now the trackpad on the other hand isn't  that great  it uses a traditional diving board  design so it's hard to click at the top  the magic keyboards trackpad is much  better with a unique design  that's not only easier to click but you  get an  even clicking feel anywhere on the  trackpad one thing for sure is that  samsung is focusing on making the tab s7  a great  laptop replacement in terms of a couple  of design choices  including making the keyboard itself  much better but one thing you'll notice  is that the front-facing webcam is no  longer on the top  it's now on the side so when you're  using it with the keyboard case  the webcam is now perfectly centered at  the top  just like a traditional laptop the main  issue with the ipad pro is that when  you're using a keyboard case  the webcam is off to the side so it  looks very awkward  almost like you're not paying attention  to the person you're talking to  check out this webcam and microphone  comparison to see what i mean  this is the video and audio quality of  the samsung galaxy tab s7  this is the video and audio quality of  the 2020 ipad pro  this design choice makes it very clear  that samsung cares a lot about the tab  s7 being a laptop replacement which  brings us to samsung's  secret sauce dex mode it basically gives  you a traditional pc like ui  that's very familiar to windows giving  you multitasking and file management  features  that absolutely kill everything the ipad  pro has to offer  especially since the tab s7 comes with a  micro sd card slot for extra storage  dex is so good that it single handedly  makes the tab s7  a much better laptop replacement than  the ipad pro  currently is and an added bonus is that  you can get 5g  on the tab s7 which you can't currently  get on the ipad pro  so that can be great for users on the go  the last thing we need to talk about  before getting into the conclusion  is the performance so let's talk about  the snapdragon 865 plus chip  compared to last year's model it's not  that much faster  but it's still the second fastest mobile  tablet as of right now  with the ipad pro staying ahead in terms  of both processor  and graphics performance however when i  compared the gaming experience using  call of duty mobile on both  the tab s7 and the ipad pro the tab was  every bit as fast giving you an  excellent gaming experience  so the extra power of the ipad pro is  simply overkill  for the apps and games we have today so  the performance of the tab seven  is more than enough for almost everyone  and you're getting that performance for  only 650 dollars  instead of 800 with the ipad pro so  you're truly getting a lot of value  especially since the s pen is included  compared to paying 130  for the 2nd gen apple pencil and on top  of that samsung's keyboard case is only  200  compared to 300 for apple's high-end  magic keyboard  so if you want to get the full tablet  experience it's gonna cost you a  thousand  two hundred and thirty dollars on the  ipad pro  and only eight hundred and fifty bucks  on the tab  s7 saving you three hundred and eighty  dollars  now of course there's a reason why  apple's ipads are the  best selling tablets out there and  that's because of the ios app store  and class leading software support which  leads to ipads holding their value  incredibly well but if you don't really  care about the software  or if you actually prefer android then  the tabber 7 gives you way  better bang for the buck especially now  that samsung's tab seven  with keyboard case bundle is currently  on sale on amazon  for only 750 dollars and you can find a  link to that sale  down in the description below but to  finally wrap up this review  i've gotta say good job samsung because  you  absolutely killed it with your new tab  s7  if you enjoy this video go ahead and tap  the like button and click the circle  above to subscribe  for more videos like this one and if you  haven't yet seen the comparisons  to the ipad pro you can watch them right  over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one
 

